# CP18.2 — one test. The presets are now tested through the endpoint.

tests/test_decide.py
checkpoints/cp18_2.allowlist

# --- F44 ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The old test read the page as text:
#
#     assert '"mandate_revoked"' in block and '"revoked"' in block
#     assert block.count('"do_not_honour"') >= 2
#     assert "tick: 16" in block
#     assert '"2026-01-25"' in block
#
# Every one of those is true of a shuffled preset list. Nothing tied tick 16 to
# the 02:00 case or the promise date to the promise case, so the two contact
# presets could swap their distinguishing values and the suite would stay green
# while both buttons demonstrated the wrong gate. The three behaviour tests
# above it are hand-built and never see a preset at all.
#
# It now builds each preset's real payload and posts it.
#
#   values <- preset.values[k] ?? DECIDE_DEFAULTS[k] ?? ""     (preset handler)
#   payload <- drop empties, "true"/"false" -> bool, number inputs -> Number
#                                                              (body())
#
# The four constants are evaluated in node rather than pattern-matched, so a
# renamed field or a preset naming a field the form does not render fails
# instead of quietly setting nothing. Then POST /policy/decide through the ASGI
# app — the route, the body parse and the validation the browser meets, not the
# in-process `decide()` the other tests call — and assert what each preset's own
# `why` claims:
#
#   Expired card          retry ABSENT from the priced options and reported as
#                         excluded by the class. Not blocked; never a candidate.
#   Bank said no, 02:00   every send_message blocked, block_gate == G1, at least
#                         one retry still legal, and ist_hour == 2.
#   Already promised      every send_message blocked, block_gate == G6, a retry
#                         still legal, and NOT in quiet hours — otherwise G1
#                         could be doing G6's work and the preset would pass
#                         while demonstrating the other gate.
#
# Checked by mutation, on a scratch copy of the page, all three restored after:
#
#   tick 16 moved to the promise preset  -> "Bank said no, 02:00: G1 blocked nothing"
#   02:00 preset back on time_shiftable  -> "no contact candidate to block"   (A151)
#   the two contact presets swapped      -> "the presets on screen are not the
#                                            ones asserted here"
#
# The second is the one worth having. It is A151 exactly — the failure that
# shipped once, silently, on the demo surface — and it now fails a test.

# --- What this still does not cover -------------------------------------------
#
# The payload is assembled by rules mirrored from the page, not by the page. A
# DOM shim rendering screen 4 and clicking the button would be the honest
# version; test_viewer.py's shim does not know the `decide` mount, which is why
# renderDecide carries its null guard. So a change to `body()`'s coercion — a
# new field kind, empties sent rather than dropped — would not be caught here.
# The mirror is nine lines and sits beside the rules it copies.
